# Cursor project rules for suwappu-lattice-protocol
# Last updated: 2026-05-16.
#
# This file scopes Cursor's suggestions to the conventions of the LTP
# codebase. Same content as CLAUDE.md and docs/AI_AGENTS.md, in the
# format Cursor expects. If you want the full agent guide, open
# docs/AI_AGENTS.md.

You are working in the Lattice Transfer Protocol (LTP) repository — a
post-quantum cryptographic data transfer protocol with three
independently-versioned surfaces: Python SDK (src/ltp/), Solidity
registry (contracts/), and the LTP-corridor-v1 wire format.

## Hard rules

- Do NOT add Co-Authored-By footers to commit messages. Repo convention.
- Do NOT use `git rebase` on shared branches. Use `git merge` or
  `git pull --no-rebase`.
- Do NOT skip hooks with `--no-verify`.
- Do NOT change a deployed-contract address in docs/DEPLOYED_CONTRACTS.md
  without an upgrade plan under plans/. CODEOWNERS will block it.
- Do NOT touch the `license` field in pyproject.toml. Resolution is
  pending in Linear GLO-785.
- SHA-pin every new GitHub Action — pin by commit SHA, not by tag (audit
  finding LTP-A-025).
- Before suggesting changes under contracts/, ensure
  `make contracts-secaudit` is green.

## Verification commands

- Python tests: `make test-python`
- Solidity tests: `make test-contracts`
- Full smart-contract security suite: `make contracts-secaudit`
- API docs: `make docs-api` (use Python 3.10–3.13; 3.14 has a pdoc bug)

## Common gotchas

- The Python package fails to import without `pqcrypto` + `pynacl`. Run
  `pip install -e '.[production]'` or work inside an appropriate venv.
- BLS DST strings must be byte-identical across Python and Solidity.
  No Unicode normalization, no trim (LTP-A-022).
- `LTP_ENV=production` triggers fail-closed paths. Don't override.

## Where to look

- Landing docs: docs/README.md (persona-routed)
- Agent guide: docs/AI_AGENTS.md
- Stability promises + version matrix: docs/STABILITY_PROMISES.md
- Operator runbook: docs/OPERATOR_RUNBOOK.md
- Latest security audit: docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_2026-05-15.md
